KG42.register("clusters-c8b879b640edb6f60d6a7dba",{"id":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v142-d-CL001","paper":"19-two_stage_battery_sharing","label":"ESC power balance and battery shared-responsibility control","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"ESC power balance and battery shared-responsibility control","market_meaning":"Under the assumption that batteries share charging and discharging responsibility in proportion to rated capacity, the ESC organizes a common control signal and is responsible for the power balance between the community and the main grid; how actual power carries out shared responsibility at SOC boundaries still needs to be clarified.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"This Rule-Chain has an independent control-responsibility meaning, but equality of normalized power depends on the shared-responsibility assumption. The source also allows individual batteries to reach the SOC boundary first, so the common signal cannot be directly interpreted as actual power being strictly proportional in all states.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"This Rule-Cluster defines the grid interface and battery control responsibility. Transaction-participation permission and ex-post pricing settlement have different inputs and outcomes and are assembled separately; being jointly under ESC responsibility is insufficient to combine these functions into one rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Centrally express main-grid balance, unidirectional control and capacity-normalized shared responsibility, retained as an independent control-responsibility rule."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence on which this Rule-Cluster relies remains unverified; permission for candidate use in the experiment does not mean that the source transcription or control interpretation has been independently verified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e002","v141-b-g01-e004","v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g02-E15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually verify the source transcription and applicable conditions; retain the current evidence status and do not treat candidate assembly as scientific acceptance."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"C004 imposes equality of normalized power on all batteries and times, whereas E15 allows batteries to reach the SOC boundary asynchronously. The current Rule-Chain does not distinguish the common instruction from constrained actual power, nor does it clarify the non-zero domain of applicability of the capacity denominator.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x001","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x002","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-theta001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e010","v141-b-g01-e011","v141-b-g02-E15"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should clarify the conditional relationship among the normalization assumption, SOC saturation and actual executed power; retain the existing C004, and do not add exceptions or alter the equality in D."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The source describes two-stage optimization, real-time correction and control boundaries, but the supplied Rule-Chain directory does not contain the corresponding complete Rule-Chains and does not give the exact object interface between the R001 individual control quantity and the subsequently aggregated allocated power.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x001","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-x002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E11","v141-b-g02-E12","v141-b-g02-E16","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If an executable scheduling rule is to be formed, C should complete the two-stage decisions, physical constraints and power interface, and verify the signs and boundaries; an equivalence mapping cannot be established merely because both are charging/discharging power."}]},"rule_refs":["19-two_stage_battery_sharing::v141-c-R001"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["KG31-fc19e7c39ea9de54"]});
